## Core Components

### 1. ZeroClaw Agent (Rust Binary)

**Location:** `src/main.rs`, `crates/zeroclaw-runtime/`

The agent is the core orchestrator that:
- Receives messages from channels/CLI/gateway
- Processes through LLM with tools
- Manages conversation context
- Executes tools safely
- Stores memories

**Key Modules:**
```
crates/zeroclaw-runtime/src/
├── agent/
│   ├── loop_.rs          # Main agent loop
│   ├── context.rs        # Context management
│   └── history.rs        # Message history
├── tools/
│   ├── mod.rs            # Tool registry
│   ├── skill_tool.rs     # Skill shell tool
│   ├── shell.rs          # Shell execution
│   └── ...               # Other tools
├── security/
│   ├── mod.rs            # Security policy
│   ├── detect.rs         # Threat detection
│   └── sandbox.rs        # Sandbox execution
├── skills/
│   ├── mod.rs            # Skill loading
│   └── registry.rs       # Skill registry
├── memory/
│   └── ...               # Memory integration
└── observability/
    └── ...               # Logging, tracing
```

### 2. Skills System

**Location:** `~/open-skills/skills/`, `crates/zeroclaw-runtime/src/skills/`

Skills are user-defined capabilities that extend the agent:

```toml
# ~/open-skills/skills/event-inference/SKILL.toml
[skill]
name = "event-inference"
description = "Analyze faces in videos to infer events"
version = "3.0.0"

prompts = [
    "What event is happening",
    "analyze this video",
    ...
]

[[tools]]
name = "analyze_media"
kind = "shell"
command = "~/.zeroclaw/venv/bin/python3 ~/.zeroclaw/video_event_analyzer.py {{file}}"
```

**How Skills Work:**
1. Skills loaded from `~/open-skills/skills/` at startup
2. Each skill's `[[tools]]` becomes a `SkillShellTool`
3. LLM can invoke skill tools by name
4. Tool executes as shell command with timeout (300s)

### 3. Tool Framework

**Location:** `crates/zeroclaw-api/src/tool.rs`, `crates/zeroclaw-tools/`

All tools implement the `Tool` trait:

```rust
#[async_trait]
pub trait Tool: Send + Sync {
    fn name(&self) -> &str;
    fn description(&self) -> &str;
    fn parameters_schema(&self) -> serde_json::Value;
    async fn execute(&self, args: serde_json::Value) -> anyhow::Result<ToolResult>;
}
```

**Built-in Tools:**
| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `shell` | Execute shell commands |
| `file_read` | Read files |
| `file_write` | Write files |
| `file_edit` | Edit files |
| `glob_search` | Search files by pattern |
| `content_search` | Search file contents |
| `memory_recall` | Retrieve memories |
| `memory_store` | Store memories |
| `browser` | Web automation |
| `web_search` | Web search |
| `web_fetch` | Fetch web pages |
| `cron_*` | Cron job management |
| `delegate` | Delegate to sub-agents |

### 4. Provider System (LLM/VLM)

**Location:** `crates/zeroclaw-api/src/provider.rs`, `crates/zeroclaw-providers/`

Providers abstract LLM/VLM APIs:

```rust
#[async_trait]
pub trait Provider: Send + Sync {
    async fn chat(&self, messages: Vec<Message>) -> Result<ChatResponse>;
    async fn chat_with_tools(&self, messages: Vec<Message>, tools: Vec<ToolSpec>) -> Result<ChatResponse>;
}
```

**Supported Providers:**
- `ollama` - Local Ollama server
- `custom` - OpenAI-compatible endpoints (llama.cpp)
- `openai` - OpenAI API
- `anthropic` - Anthropic API
- `google` - Google AI
- `azure` - Azure OpenAI

**Provider Configuration:**
```toml
[providers]
fallback = "custom:http://localhost:8000/v1"

[providers.models."custom:http://localhost:8000/v1"]
model = "qwen-vl"
base_url = "http://localhost:8000/v1"
api_key = "not-needed"
```

### 5. Memory System

**Location:** `crates/zeroclaw-api/src/memory_traits.rs`, `crates/zeroclaw-memory/`

Memory backends implement the `Memory` trait:

```rust
#[async_trait]
pub trait Memory: Send + Sync {
    async fn store(&self, entry: MemoryEntry) -> Result<String>;
    async fn recall(&self, query: &str, namespace: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<MemoryEntry>>;
    async fn delete(&self, id: &str) -> Result<()>;
    async fn hygiene(&self) -> Result<HygieneReport>;
}
```

**Memory Backends:**
| Backend | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `sqlite` | SQLite database (default) |
| `markdown` | Markdown files |
| `postgres` | PostgreSQL with pgvector |
| `qdrant` | Qdrant vector database |
| `embeddings` | Embedding-based retrieval |
| `vector_merge` | Hybrid vector + keyword |

### 6. Channel System

**Location:** `crates/zeroclaw-api/src/channel.rs`, `crates/zeroclaw-channels/`

Channels are messaging platform integrations:

```rust
#[async_trait]
pub trait Channel: Send + Sync {
    async fn connect(&self) -> Result<()>;
    async fn send(&self, message: ChannelMessage) -> Result<()>;
    async fn disconnect(&self) -> Result<()>;
}
```

**Supported Channels (30+):**
- Slack
- Discord
- Telegram
- WhatsApp
- Microsoft Teams
- Email (IMAP/SMTP)
- SMS (Twilio)
- LINE
- WeChat
- And more...

### 7. Gateway API

**Location:** `crates/zeroclaw-gateway/`

REST/WebSocket API for external integration:

**Endpoints:**
```
POST   /api/v1/pair          - Pair new device
POST   /api/v1/webhook       - Webhook receiver
GET    /api/v1/sessions      - List sessions
POST   /api/v1/sessions      - Create session
GET    /api/v1/sessions/:id  - Get session
POST   /api/v1/sessions/:id/messages  - Send message
WS     /ws/chat              - WebSocket chat
```

**Authentication:**
- Pairing code flow for new devices
- Token-based authentication
- Rate limiting per token

### 8. Security System

**Location:** `crates/zeroclaw-runtime/src/security/`

**Components:**
| Component | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `SecurityPolicy` | Access control rules |
| `Sandbox` | Command sandboxing |
| `ResourceMonitor` | CPU/memory limits |
| `AuditLogger` | Action logging |
| `OTP` | Two-factor auth |
| `EStop` | Emergency stop |

**Security Levels:**
```toml
[security]
autonomy = "full"  # none, ask, full
workspace_only = true
allowed_commands = ["git", "npm", "cargo", ...]
forbidden_paths = ["/etc", "/root", ...]
```

