## Data Flow

### Request Lifecycle

```
1. User sends message via Channel/CLI/Gateway
         │
         ▼
2. Channel receives and wraps in ChannelMessage
         │
         ▼
3. Agent Loop processes message
   - Load conversation history
   - Add user message to context
   - Trim context if needed (32K token budget)
         │
         ▼
4. LLM receives messages + available tools
   - Provider formats request
   - Sends to LLM API
         │
         ▼
5. LLM responds with:
   - Text response, OR
   - Tool call request
         │
         ▼
6. If Tool Call:
   - Parse tool name and arguments
   - Look up tool in registry
   - Validate against security policy
   - Execute tool (with timeout)
   - Return result to LLM
   - Go to step 4 (iterate up to 10 times)
         │
         ▼
7. If Text Response:
   - Send to channel for delivery
   - Store in memory (if enabled)
   - Update conversation history
```

### Tool Execution Flow

```
Tool Call Received
         │
         ▼
Security Validation
- Check autonomy level
- Validate command (if shell)
- Check forbidden paths
- Rate limit check
         │
         ▼
Execute Tool
- ShellTool: Run in sandbox
- SkillShellTool: Run with 300s timeout
- File tools: Path validation
- Memory tools: Backend operations
         │
         ▼
Capture Output
- stdout/stderr (max 1MB)
- Exit code
- Execution time
         │
         ▼
Return ToolResult
- success: bool
- output: String
- error: Option<String>
         │
         ▼
Log to Audit (if enabled)
- Action type
- Arguments (sanitized)
- Result
- Timestamp
```

### Memory Operations

```
Store Memory
    │
    ▼
Validate Entry
- Content length
- Namespace exists
- Category valid
    │
    ▼
Backend-Specific Storage
- SQLite: INSERT INTO memories
- Markdown: Write to file
- Postgres: INSERT with embedding
    │
    ▼
Return Memory ID
```

```
Recall Memory
    │
    ▼
Parse Query
- Extract keywords
- Generate embedding (if hybrid)
    │
    ▼
Backend-Specific Search
- SQLite: FTS5 + metadata filter
- Vector: Cosine similarity
- Hybrid: Combine scores
    │
    ▼
Rank and Filter
- Relevance threshold (0.4 default)
- Max results
- Namespace filter
    │
    ▼
Return Memory Entries
```

