## Deployment

### Build from Source

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.sec.samsung.net/vdil-data/zeroClaw_POC.git
cd zeroClaw_POC

# Build release binary
cargo build --release

# Install binary
cp target/release/zeroclaw ~/.cargo/bin/
```

### Install via Script

```bash
# Run installer
./install.sh

# This will:
# 1. Build zeroclaw binary
# 2. Create ~/.zeroclaw directory
# 3. Generate default config
# 4. Set up Python venv
# 5. Install Python dependencies
```

### Runtime Requirements

**System:**
- macOS 12+ or Linux
- 8GB RAM minimum (16GB recommended)
- 10GB disk space

**Dependencies:**
- Rust 1.70+
- Python 3.10+
- OpenCV (for video analysis)
- SQLite3

**VLM Server:**
- SSH tunnel to remote server
- llama.cpp or Ollama running
- qwen-vl model loaded

### SSH Tunnel Setup

```bash
# Start tunnel (keep running)
ssh -L 8000:localhost:8000 joonyeoup.k1@105.145.80.65

# Test connection
curl http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"qwen-vl","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"hi"}]}]}'
```

### First Run

```bash
# Run onboarding wizard
zeroclaw onboard

# Or manually configure:
# 1. Edit ~/.zeroclaw/config.toml
# 2. Set up providers
# 3. Configure channels
# 4. Enable skills

# Start agent
zeroclaw agent

# Or run CLI command
zeroclaw agent -m "Hello, what can you do?"
```

